" "step-103728c3-da2e-5746-827f-d6cd0408ce21"] :activity/first-step "step-e0417e83-32c0-51c3-9fdf-a23975370a1f" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-e0417e83-32c0-51c3-9fdf-a23975370a1f" :step/id #uuid "e0417e83-32c0-51c3-9fdf-a23975370a1f" :step/content 17592186193377 :step/next "step-fc7a8ece-f5fa-5dfb-a44a-4b9b848e5eef" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-fc7a8ece-f5fa-5dfb-a44a-4b9b848e5eef" :step/id #uuid "fc7a8ece-f5fa-5dfb-a44a-4b9b848e5eef" :step/content 17592186479881 :step/next "step-d4a32acc-c162-55a3-84e9-b8804219af5e" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-d4a32acc-c162-55a3-84e9-b8804219af5e" :step/id #uuid "d4a32acc-c162-55a3-84e9-b8804219af5e" :step/content 17592186479858 :step/next "step-1d9ba6fc-d1ed-5998-a6a1-15240e008963" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-1d9ba6fc-d1ed-5998-a6a1-15240e008963" :step/id #uuid "1d9ba6fc-d1ed-5998-a6a1-15240e008963" :step/content 17592186278579 :step/next "step-103728c3-da2e-5746-827f-d6cd0408ce21" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-103728c3-da2e-5746-827f-d6cd0408ce21" :step/id #uuid "103728c3-da2e-5746-827f-d6cd0408ce21" :step/content 17592186278581 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186228916 :question/problem "![](images/3d/3db7e4a714d16b8f150bbca5fc9e60fdbf30da038e7dbf331dc317d6ec7c8c3c.svg)\nFill in the blanks in the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ![](images/e7/e7b8344a953c494431f7c9594dbe6124e2e4264c3d58bc94fa383323fc85389d.svg) where ![](images/d3/d3a5e4fd69f446e59007f8e3f8c982b424deedcb837670b75c5342968b7e0549.svg)*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{XXXX}}\\, \\\\ 3{e}^{4(t-1)}\\end{aligned}]+{\\int }_{1}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4t} \\\\ \\,\\,\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{XX}}\\,\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given the system $\\mathbf{x}'(t) = A \\mathbf{x}(t)+\\mathbf{g}(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\underbrace{e^{A(t-t_0)} \\, \\mathbf{x}(t_0)}_{\\text{homogeneous part}} + \\underbrace{\\int_{t_0}^{t} e^{A(t-s)} \\mathbf{g}(s) \\, \\text{d}s}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x(t_0)$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ![](images/7b/7b64128fdaf3565ee121779a8fcd2c84db8f639ded96f0884d6ad7e728c83b1c.svg) So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4(t-1)} & (t-1){e}^{4(t-1)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4(t-1)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3(t-1){e}^{4(t-1)} \\\\ 3{e}^{4(t-1)}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n![](images/7f/7f1779e39ecb5e2bcce580d20a85eae97be505e2ad0987fa45b5b9e22c52fbbf.svg)\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{4(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4(t-s)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4s} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}3(t-1){e}^{4(t-1)} \\\\ 3{e}^{4(t-1)}\\end{aligned}]+{\\int }_{1}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186230191 :tutorial/content "Matrix exponentials can be used for solving *inhomogeneous systems* of ODEs as well. Consider the system\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t)+\\mathbf{g}(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is a constant square matrix, and suppose we are given an initial condition $\\mathbf{x}(t_0)$.\n\nOur goal is to derive the formula for the solution $\\mathbf{x}(t)$ of the system.\n\nFirst, we eliminate the *inhomogeneous term* by a change of variables. We define\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{y}(t)=e^{-A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t)\n$$\n\nand differentiate it using the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =({e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})})^{′}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}{x}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(-A){e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}(Ax(t)+g(t)) \\\\  & =\\cancel{-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)}+\\cancel{A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)}+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}g(t) \\\\  & ={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}g(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate both sides from $t_0$ to $t$ and get\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{y}(t)-\\mathbf{y}(t_0)=\\int_{t_0}^{t} e^{-A(s-t_0)}\\mathbf{g}(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nNext, since $\\mathbf{y}(t_0)=e^{-A(t_0-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t_0)=\\mathbf{x}(t_0),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{y}(t)=\\mathbf{x}(t_0)+\\int_{t_0}^{t} e^{-A(s-t_0)}\\mathbf{g}(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nFinally, we convert back to the initial variable $\\mathbf{x}(t).$ To do that we multiply both sides by $e^{A(t-t_0)}{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t) & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\ x(t) & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to our IVP is\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\underbrace{e^{A(t-t_0)} \\, \\mathbf{x}(t_0)}_{\\text{homogeneous part}} + \\underbrace{\\int_{t_0}^{t} e^{A(t-s)} \\mathbf{g}(s) \\, \\text{d}s}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere the first term represents the solution of the corresponding *homogeneous system*, and the second term gives a particular solution of our *inhomogeneous system*.\n\nLet's see some concrete examples." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186229257 :activity/expected-seconds 1440.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "activity-3c12d8df-59d7-51f9-9588-92c3d42e2238" :activity/id #uuid "3c12d8df-59d7-51f9-9588-92c3d42e2238" :activity/title "Equality of Mixed Partial Derivatives" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049696 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-7f5bbb0a-88b6-5f7d-9f06-8a26f6ee53a3" "step-0330742a-33ff-5afc-89cc-0f92fa6fe78f" "step-a01dfe7c-004d-5b4b-a3ba-f0b7986950c5" "step-efa110b9-bada-584b-9f76-02913ac29d55" "step-dce668a8-ef22-5a60-bb9c-32f6ba050503"] :activity/first-step "step-7f5bbb0a-88b6-5f7d-9f06-8a26f6ee53a3" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-7f5bbb0a-88b6-5f7d-9f06-8a26f6ee53a3" :step/id #uuid "7f5bbb0a-88b6-5f7d-9f06-8a26f6ee53a3" :step/content 17592186124999 :step/next "step-0330742a-33ff-5afc-89cc-0f92fa6fe78f" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-0330742a-33ff-5afc-89cc-0f92fa6fe78f" :step/id #uuid "0330742a-33ff-5afc-89cc-0f92fa6fe78f" :step/content 17592186479833 :step/next "step-a01dfe7c-004d-5b4b-a3ba-f0b7986950c5" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-a01dfe7c-004d-5b4b-a3ba-f0b7986950c5" :step/id #uuid "a01dfe7c-004d-5b4b-a3ba-f0b7986950c5" :step/content 17592186479870 :step/next "step-efa110b9-bada-584b-9f76-02913ac29d55" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-efa110b9-bada-584b-9f76-02913ac29d55" :step/id #uuid "efa110b9-bada-584b-9f76-02913ac29d55" :step/content 17592186348445 :step/next "step-dce668a8-ef22-5a60-bb9c-32f6ba050503" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-dce668a8-ef22-5a60-bb9c-32f6ba050503" :step/id #uuid "dce668a8-ef22-5a60-bb9c-32f6ba050503" :step/content 17592186409651 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "activity-3a312771-af16-5ebc-966b-7a48dcb2b02c" :activity/id #uuid "3a312771-af16-5ebc-966b-7a48dcb2b02c" :activity/title "Convergence of Fourier Series" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050989 :activity/course 17592186046660 :activity/steps ["step-648c2889-db3b-5dfc-94a8-f9019704bcd0" "step-00120d36-1a04-5461-a0b6-aa8a3c9fb95d" "step